{"path":"memory/unique_ptr/operator*","title":"std::unique_ptr<T,Deleter>::operator*, std::unique_ptr<T,Deleter>::operator->","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::unique_ptr&lt;T,Deleter&gt;::</span>operator*, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::unique_ptr&lt;T,Deleter&gt;::</span>operator-&gt;","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr/operator*","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"operator* and operator-> provide access to the object owned by *this.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/add_reference\"><span class=\"kw613\">std::<span class=\"me2\">add_lvalue_reference</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">type</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/declval\"><span class=\"kw1128\">std::<span class=\"me2\">declval</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>pointer<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark\">(constexpr since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pointer operator<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark\">(constexpr since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>operator*</code> and <code>operator-&gt;</code> provide access to the object owned by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>.\n</p><p>The behavior is undefined if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">get<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> nullptr</span></code>.\n</p><p>These member functions are only provided for <code>unique_ptr</code> for the single objects i.e. the primary template.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Returns the object owned by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>, equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>get<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Returns a pointer to the object owned by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>, i.e. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">get<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> May throw if <code>pointer</code> has a throwing <code>operator*</code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The use of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/add_reference\">std::add_lvalue_reference</a></span> is to make it possible to instantiate <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr\"><span class=\"kw737\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unique_ptr</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> since <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> isn't allowed in C++ while <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/add_reference\"><span class=\"kw613\">std::<span class=\"me2\">add_lvalue_reference</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> produces <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span></span></code>. See <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue673\" data-external=\"1\">LWG673</a> for details.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;memory&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> Foo\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> bar<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Foo::bar<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> f<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Foo<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> \n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"f(const Foo&amp;)<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> \n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr\"><span class=\"kw737\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unique_ptr</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Foo<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> ptr<span class=\"br0\">(</span>new Foo<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    ptr<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>bar<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    f<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>ptr<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Foo::bar\nf(const Foo&amp;)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2762\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2762</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++11\n</td>\n<td><code>operator*</code> might be potentially-throwing even if<br><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>get<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> was noexcept\n</td>\n<td>a conditional exception specification added\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr/get\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>get</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns a pointer to the managed object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"},{"path":"memory/unique_ptr","title":"std::unique_ptr"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::unique_ptr<T,Deleter>::operator*, std::unique_ptr<T,Deleter>::operator->","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++11. operator* and operator-> provide access to the object owned by *this."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Returns the object owned by *this, equivalent to *get()."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"May throw if pointer has a throwing operator*."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The use of std::add_lvalue_reference is to make it possible to instantiate std::unique_ptr<void> since void& isn't allowed in C++ while…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"get","note":"returns a pointer to the managed object"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":209,"codeBlockCount":2}
